1
00:01:30,470 --> 00:01:34,979
[AWAKEN]

2
00:01:35,550 --> 00:01:37,950
[Episode 16]

3
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:04,180
It was you who tipped off Du Huangqiao

4
00:02:05,180 --> 00:02:07,840
that we were holding a meeting
in the Fairy Bath.

5
00:02:12,590 --> 00:02:14,030
Whether it was me or not,

6
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:17,329
they all died because of me.

7
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:20,420
I accept the blame.

8
00:02:25,590 --> 00:02:29,250
The Western Zhejiang Training Class
failed to teach you loyalty,

9
00:02:30,740 --> 00:02:33,670
but it taught you all too well
how to be cold-blooded.

10
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:37,150
How ironic.

11
00:02:39,870 --> 00:02:42,000
I know you're very disappointed in me.

12
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:45,360
I'm disappointed in myself too.

13
00:02:45,910 --> 00:02:46,640
Back then...

14
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:50,880
I should've let you die in Yangzhou.

15
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:07,510
♪ I have a little sister named Jiumei ♪

16
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:13,310
♪ She's clever and bright,
admired by all ♪

17
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:16,310
No matter who it is,
no matter what it's about,

18
00:03:16,310 --> 00:03:17,870
don't let anyone disturb me.

19
00:03:17,870 --> 00:03:18,560
Yes, sir.

20
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:20,620
Sing in a private room?

21
00:03:21,630 --> 00:03:22,870
What do they take us for?

22
00:03:22,870 --> 00:03:23,800
We're not going!

23
00:03:24,700 --> 00:03:26,700
Then go tell the Japanese yourself.

24
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:28,710
Our little troupe

25
00:03:28,900 --> 00:03:30,500
can't afford to offend them.

26
00:03:30,950 --> 00:03:32,320
I came from the Northeast.

27
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:33,890
I've seen plenty of Japanese.

28
00:03:33,890 --> 00:03:34,610
I'll go.

29
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:35,460
You're still young.

30
00:03:35,460 --> 00:03:36,390
I'll go instead.

31
00:03:36,910 --> 00:03:37,840
I'll go with you.

32
00:03:38,410 --> 00:03:39,620
Be good. Wait here.

33
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:40,900
Let's go.

34
00:03:47,150 --> 00:03:48,870
Cigarettes! Cigarettes!

35
00:03:50,370 --> 00:03:52,630
Sir, would you like a pack of cigarettes?

36
00:03:55,470 --> 00:03:56,329
Thank you, sir.

37
00:03:58,500 --> 00:03:59,360
Save her.

38
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:01,120
Cigarettes!

39
00:04:01,590 --> 00:04:03,520
Cigarettes, cigarettes!

40
00:04:05,840 --> 00:04:06,910
Stop struggling!

41
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:08,150
Let go of me!

42
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:30,360
Work for me.

43
00:04:33,190 --> 00:04:33,950
Will you?

44
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:49,430
We gave you a chance,

45
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:52,280
gave you a gun,

46
00:04:53,780 --> 00:04:55,550
and let you kill your enemies.

47
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:01,420
But what did you do?

48
00:05:02,190 --> 00:05:03,430
You turned the barrel

49
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:06,280
on the very people who saved you.

50
00:05:11,560 --> 00:05:12,520
I can no longer

51
00:05:13,310 --> 00:05:15,240
live only for myself.

52
00:05:17,670 --> 00:05:18,560
A true warrior

53
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:20,690
is never meant to live for themselves!

54
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:31,980
I don't have the same lofty ideals as you.

55
00:05:34,510 --> 00:05:35,360
Captain Tao.

56
00:05:37,630 --> 00:05:38,830
You have a family too.

57
00:05:49,110 --> 00:05:50,110
I'm begging you.

58
00:05:51,180 --> 00:05:52,150
Let us go.

59
00:06:05,520 --> 00:06:06,350
Please.

60
00:06:18,110 --> 00:06:20,170
You have a family to protect too, huh?

61
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:25,630
My 12 comrades...

62
00:06:28,270 --> 00:06:29,870
They had families too.

63
00:06:33,159 --> 00:06:35,159
They were someone's parents,

64
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:37,920
someone's children too.

65
00:06:44,750 --> 00:06:45,510
I know.

66
00:06:49,070 --> 00:06:50,830
No matter what I say or do,

67
00:06:53,390 --> 00:06:55,920
I can never atone
for the sins I've committed.

68
00:07:00,260 --> 00:07:02,260
Could you give me a little more time?

69
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:05,960
Let me give birth to my child.

70
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:14,940
Then I'll come to you
to atone for my sins.

71
00:07:24,190 --> 00:07:25,650
You alone won't be enough.

72
00:07:29,130 --> 00:07:30,860
Du Huangqiao has to pay too.

73
00:07:36,510 --> 00:07:37,909
Among my 12 comrades...

74
00:07:40,270 --> 00:07:41,430
there was a boy.

75
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:44,190
He...

76
00:07:45,030 --> 00:07:47,270
He was only 15.

77
00:07:49,610 --> 00:07:51,090
He was only 15!

78
00:08:13,300 --> 00:08:15,360
Don't you want to atone for your sins?

79
00:08:17,320 --> 00:08:17,960
Fine.

80
00:08:28,930 --> 00:08:30,120
Kill Du Huangqiao.

81
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:37,669
Why does it have to be me?

82
00:08:39,789 --> 00:08:41,590
That's what God of Wealth wants.

83
00:08:50,410 --> 00:08:51,210
She said...

84
00:08:53,850 --> 00:08:55,580
she'd give you one more chance.

85
00:08:58,670 --> 00:09:00,470
Only if you kill Du Huangqiao...

86
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:08,480
will your child get to see the world.

87
00:09:28,030 --> 00:09:29,430
You don't have much time.

88
00:09:35,260 --> 00:09:36,300
Make your choice.

89
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:53,210
Chen Kailai.

90
00:09:53,830 --> 00:09:55,320
The captain needs your help.

91
00:09:55,320 --> 00:09:55,920
What for?

92
00:09:57,070 --> 00:09:58,070
Just come with me.

93
00:10:12,910 --> 00:10:13,570
Captain Du.

94
00:10:14,740 --> 00:10:16,870
I need to interrogate some prisoners.

95
00:10:19,560 --> 00:10:20,360
Open the door.

96
00:10:24,230 --> 00:10:25,030
Open the door.

97
00:10:36,040 --> 00:10:38,100
Take them to the interrogation room.

98
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:41,980
Captain Du,

99
00:10:42,390 --> 00:10:44,320
you still need to sign a few papers.

100
00:10:44,510 --> 00:10:45,080
Let's go.

101
00:10:47,850 --> 00:10:48,580
Chen Kailai.

102
00:10:49,510 --> 00:10:50,150
This way.

103
00:10:51,870 --> 00:10:52,670
Listen to me.

104
00:11:22,710 --> 00:11:23,360
Hurry up.

105
00:11:28,190 --> 00:11:28,910
Hurry.

106
00:11:37,670 --> 00:11:39,070
Get them in the car first.

107
00:11:53,670 --> 00:11:54,400
Follow them.

108
00:11:54,460 --> 00:11:55,190
Understood.

109
00:12:04,550 --> 00:12:05,200
Director,

110
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:08,200
under the guise of interrogation,
Du Huangqiao

111
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:09,930
took away 3 key NBIS prisoners.

112
00:12:10,670 --> 00:12:12,270
We don't know what he's up to.

113
00:12:12,870 --> 00:12:13,440
Yes.

114
00:12:18,700 --> 00:12:19,660
Du the Blind...

115
00:12:29,430 --> 00:12:31,160
What exactly are we going to do?

116
00:12:33,430 --> 00:12:36,090
My wife has been captured
by the Hurricane Team.

117
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:38,330
We're going to trade them for her life.

118
00:12:45,070 --> 00:12:47,120
If anything happens to her,

119
00:12:48,200 --> 00:12:49,560
no one gets to live.

120
00:13:21,430 --> 00:13:23,290
You'd better think this through.

121
00:13:39,180 --> 00:13:40,260
Tell me,

122
00:13:41,690 --> 00:13:43,260
could this be a trap?

123
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:49,400
Then why did you still go?

124
00:13:51,330 --> 00:13:52,730
My life is worth nothing,

125
00:13:54,270 --> 00:13:56,870
but she and our child must live on.

126
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:01,970
Chen Kailai.

127
00:14:04,750 --> 00:14:06,210
You have to do right by her.

128
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:07,960
If I die,

129
00:14:09,780 --> 00:14:12,180
you must take good care
of her and the child.

130
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:21,930
Are you alright?

131
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:27,270
I think he kicked.

132
00:16:28,210 --> 00:16:29,540
I wonder if he's hungry.

133
00:16:37,530 --> 00:16:38,140
Let's go.

134
00:16:39,750 --> 00:16:40,550
Let's go home.

135
00:16:44,190 --> 00:16:45,040
I'll cook.

136
00:16:47,870 --> 00:16:50,870
I stir-fried some amaranth for you
before I left yesterday.

137
00:16:50,870 --> 00:16:53,000
Amaranth is so hard to find these days.

138
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:55,010
I wonder if it's gone bad by now.

139
00:16:57,940 --> 00:16:59,400
Even if it has, I'll eat it.

140
00:17:09,680 --> 00:17:10,680
Oh, you...

141
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:13,000
Why are you so silly?

142
00:17:28,470 --> 00:17:29,880
We can't go home.

143
00:17:44,510 --> 00:17:46,110
As long as you can live...

144
00:17:48,880 --> 00:17:50,140
and our child can live,

145
00:17:52,480 --> 00:17:53,740
just pull the trigger.

146
00:18:05,190 --> 00:18:07,070
I can't do it.

147
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:19,440
I've betrayed the Party.

148
00:18:20,600 --> 00:18:22,470
Now I've betrayed our family too.

149
00:18:24,510 --> 00:18:26,510
What's the point of living anymore?

150
00:18:30,480 --> 00:18:31,650
Live on.

151
00:18:34,570 --> 00:18:36,200
Live and raise our child.

152
00:18:39,010 --> 00:18:40,900
With no father or mother,

153
00:18:43,070 --> 00:18:45,780
he'll suffer so much.

154
00:18:56,350 --> 00:18:58,550
Then we'll just take it one day at a time.

155
00:18:59,920 --> 00:19:00,850
If we have to die,

156
00:19:01,340 --> 00:19:02,740
we'll die together.

157
00:19:06,340 --> 00:19:06,940
Let's go!

158
00:19:14,980 --> 00:19:16,240
Get in the car quickly!

159
00:19:54,680 --> 00:19:56,680
Xiaoxian! Xiaoxian!

160
00:20:58,860 --> 00:21:02,390
She was the best sniper
in the Western Zhejiang Training Class.

161
00:21:02,890 --> 00:21:06,620
She knew from the start that someone would
be hiding there to shoot.

162
00:21:15,160 --> 00:21:17,160
She was dead set on saving him.

163
00:21:18,660 --> 00:21:20,990
You never should've given her the chance.

164
00:21:21,680 --> 00:21:22,440
But she...

165
00:21:24,790 --> 00:21:26,120
was my auntie.

166
00:21:49,070 --> 00:21:51,200
This is the rice we saved
for the New Year.

167
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:52,500
You'd better get well soon.

168
00:21:52,500 --> 00:21:54,630
The troupe doesn't keep freeloaders.

169
00:21:56,790 --> 00:21:58,190
Where are you from again?

170
00:21:59,200 --> 00:22:00,330
From the Northeast.

171
00:22:00,840 --> 00:22:01,840
The Northeast...

172
00:22:02,830 --> 00:22:04,760
You came all this way to sing opera?

173
00:22:06,790 --> 00:22:07,850
My family all died.

174
00:22:08,510 --> 00:22:09,570
Because of the war.

175
00:22:15,790 --> 00:22:17,360
I've been performing here for 10 years.

176
00:22:17,360 --> 00:22:19,370
You can call me Auntie from now on.

177
00:22:31,750 --> 00:22:32,880
Do you regret it?

178
00:22:36,960 --> 00:22:37,830
Regret?

179
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:41,890
A debt...

180
00:22:43,950 --> 00:22:45,480
must be repaid eventually.

181
00:23:31,150 --> 00:23:32,260
Tie him up.

182
00:23:35,950 --> 00:23:36,590
Who?

183
00:23:39,110 --> 00:23:39,830
Him!

184
00:23:46,840 --> 00:23:47,950
Before you came...

185
00:23:49,900 --> 00:23:51,300
she was living just fine.

186
00:23:52,950 --> 00:23:53,880
Then you came...

187
00:23:55,400 --> 00:23:56,920
and she died!

188
00:24:16,720 --> 00:24:18,890
I treated you as my closest brother,

189
00:24:21,260 --> 00:24:23,540
but you sold me out.

190
00:24:29,110 --> 00:24:30,910
What exactly is your connection

191
00:24:32,270 --> 00:24:34,350
to the Hurricane Team?

192
00:24:36,160 --> 00:24:37,050
It wasn't me.

193
00:24:38,270 --> 00:24:39,830
Auntie was so good to me.

194
00:24:40,180 --> 00:24:41,580
I could never betray her.

195
00:24:41,790 --> 00:24:43,550
Then how did they find her?

196
00:24:43,710 --> 00:24:45,310
How did they find her?

197
00:24:45,330 --> 00:24:46,220
I don't know.

198
00:24:46,500 --> 00:24:47,350
I don't know!

199
00:24:50,750 --> 00:24:52,010
Betraying your mentor

200
00:24:53,400 --> 00:24:54,730
is punishable by death!

201
00:24:56,790 --> 00:24:57,720
Du Huangqiao,

202
00:24:58,710 --> 00:25:00,200
you're just a mad dog now—

203
00:25:00,690 --> 00:25:02,890
a mad dog that bites anyone in your path!

204
00:25:03,430 --> 00:25:04,360
I'm telling you,

205
00:25:04,800 --> 00:25:06,230
even if I betrayed you,

206
00:25:07,360 --> 00:25:09,120
I'd never betray Auntie.

207
00:25:26,550 --> 00:25:27,460
You're right.

208
00:25:29,410 --> 00:25:31,270
I deserve to die more than she did.

209
00:25:32,290 --> 00:25:34,420
I deserve to die more than she ever did.

210
00:25:52,590 --> 00:25:53,480
This world...

211
00:25:55,720 --> 00:25:57,380
has no shred of humanity left.

212
00:26:03,920 --> 00:26:06,350
Then no one gets to live in peace.

213
00:26:10,070 --> 00:26:12,270
Are you still going to carry on your feud

214
00:26:12,720 --> 00:26:14,120
with the Hurricane Team?

215
00:26:17,030 --> 00:26:18,690
Who will be the next to suffer?

216
00:26:25,030 --> 00:26:27,240
With wine in hand,

217
00:26:28,720 --> 00:26:31,640
who cares about the name I leave behind?

218
00:26:52,110 --> 00:26:53,640
Was it you who shot

219
00:26:54,640 --> 00:26:55,700
and killed Auntie?

220
00:27:02,110 --> 00:27:02,880
Answer me.

221
00:27:09,510 --> 00:27:10,350
Why?

222
00:27:12,040 --> 00:27:13,240
She was a traitor.

223
00:27:14,160 --> 00:27:15,030
She had to die.

224
00:27:19,960 --> 00:27:21,960
How did you know she was still alive?

225
00:27:23,830 --> 00:27:25,830
You knew that all along, didn't you?

226
00:27:27,070 --> 00:27:28,510
If I had told you earlier,

227
00:27:29,720 --> 00:27:32,120
would the outcome have been any different?

228
00:27:33,040 --> 00:27:33,650
No.

229
00:27:38,310 --> 00:27:40,480
How could you bring yourself to do it?

230
00:27:44,970 --> 00:27:46,060
Twelve lives.

231
00:27:47,160 --> 00:27:48,360
That's what she owed.

232
00:27:48,430 --> 00:27:50,190
But she was carrying a child!

233
00:27:50,680 --> 00:27:51,750
Did you know that?

234
00:27:52,030 --> 00:27:53,560
It was because of that child

235
00:27:54,230 --> 00:27:55,740
that she betrayed the Party

236
00:27:55,740 --> 00:27:56,740
and lost her life.

237
00:28:00,550 --> 00:28:03,080
I think people are better off
without a heart.

238
00:28:05,400 --> 00:28:08,000
I think you're
the most heartless person here.

239
00:28:11,830 --> 00:28:13,030
I am heartless.

240
00:28:16,160 --> 00:28:18,290
You've deceived me again and again...

241
00:28:19,160 --> 00:28:20,620
But I've never harmed you.

242
00:28:22,310 --> 00:28:24,440
Still, I always have a premonition...

243
00:28:28,030 --> 00:28:30,160
sooner or later, I'll die by your hand.

244
00:28:48,350 --> 00:28:49,880
Light some incense for her.

245
00:29:10,440 --> 00:29:11,270
Tell me...

246
00:29:14,510 --> 00:29:16,040
is this memorial tablet...

247
00:29:17,920 --> 00:29:19,310
a little too ominous?

248
00:29:21,440 --> 00:29:22,350
Auntie...

249
00:29:25,920 --> 00:29:27,380
died in the end, after all.

250
00:29:38,090 --> 00:29:39,440
I don't want to see...

251
00:29:41,600 --> 00:29:43,530
your memorial tablet here one day.

252
00:29:45,110 --> 00:29:46,200
So, Chen Kailai...

253
00:29:48,520 --> 00:29:49,890
you'd better join us.

254
00:29:53,160 --> 00:29:56,090
Otherwise, you'll either be killed
by Tao Dachun...

255
00:29:57,640 --> 00:29:59,360
or murdered by Du Huangqiao.

256
00:30:03,030 --> 00:30:04,270
I can't do

257
00:30:05,680 --> 00:30:06,750
the things you do.

258
00:30:11,880 --> 00:30:13,210
You're afraid of death?

259
00:30:14,920 --> 00:30:15,590
I am.

260
00:30:17,640 --> 00:30:18,590
Terrified.

261
00:30:22,000 --> 00:30:23,130
I have to stay alive.

262
00:30:24,550 --> 00:30:25,550
At the very least,

263
00:30:26,680 --> 00:30:28,070
I can't die before you.

264
00:30:29,920 --> 00:30:31,520
I still have to plant flowers

265
00:30:32,550 --> 00:30:33,680
at your grave

266
00:30:34,430 --> 00:30:35,690
and bring you wontons.

267
00:30:37,880 --> 00:30:39,410
I have to put all your photos

268
00:30:40,880 --> 00:30:42,200
in the display window

269
00:30:44,240 --> 00:30:45,640
so everyone can see them.

270
00:30:49,480 --> 00:30:51,080
I don't want you to become...

271
00:30:53,310 --> 00:30:55,240
a lonely wandering ghost someday.

272
00:31:15,590 --> 00:31:16,510
Chen Kailai.

273
00:31:21,510 --> 00:31:23,510
How can you be such a good liar?

274
00:31:35,640 --> 00:31:37,130
If only there were no war.

275
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:49,730
That day will come eventually.

276
00:31:53,350 --> 00:31:54,200
Director,

277
00:31:54,980 --> 00:31:57,240
I've been driving around for 3 whole days

278
00:31:57,920 --> 00:31:59,780
and burned through an entire tank of gas,

279
00:31:59,780 --> 00:32:02,510
but I haven't even
caught a glimpse of Captain Du.

280
00:32:04,270 --> 00:32:05,030
Do you think

281
00:32:05,550 --> 00:32:07,110
he drank too much

282
00:32:07,800 --> 00:32:10,190
and stumbled straight into Suzhou Creek?

283
00:32:20,680 --> 00:32:21,480
Move!

284
00:32:26,590 --> 00:32:27,310
Where is he?

285
00:32:32,200 --> 00:32:32,960
Sir,

286
00:32:33,440 --> 00:32:35,110
what bank issued this bill?

287
00:32:37,070 --> 00:32:37,790
Tell me!

288
00:32:38,160 --> 00:32:39,000
Where is he?

289
00:32:39,070 --> 00:32:40,790
I don't know what you're talking about!

290
00:32:40,790 --> 00:32:42,480
Where is he? Where is he?

291
00:32:42,510 --> 00:32:44,200
Where is he? Where is he?

292
00:32:48,070 --> 00:32:49,310
Tell me!

293
00:33:10,680 --> 00:33:11,270
Freeze!

294
00:33:12,960 --> 00:33:13,620
Don't move!

295
00:33:14,830 --> 00:33:15,350
Freeze!

296
00:33:16,070 --> 00:33:16,730
Don't move!

297
00:33:39,790 --> 00:33:41,920
The man in the photo is Feng Shen.

298
00:33:42,310 --> 00:33:43,440
He's a Communist.

299
00:33:44,270 --> 00:33:45,920
He's been studying abroad

300
00:33:46,000 --> 00:33:48,230
and has recently returned to Jiaxing
to visit relatives.

301
00:33:48,230 --> 00:33:49,690
His next stop is Shanghai.

302
00:33:51,030 --> 00:33:52,090
His contact there

303
00:33:52,880 --> 00:33:53,920
is Diana.

304
00:33:55,030 --> 00:33:56,810
How reliable is the information?

305
00:33:56,810 --> 00:33:58,070
Absolutely reliable.

306
00:33:58,920 --> 00:33:59,960
I turned

307
00:34:00,160 --> 00:34:02,490
one of the Communist Party's
liaison officers in Jiaxing.

308
00:34:02,490 --> 00:34:05,050
He's been undercover for a long time,

309
00:34:05,640 --> 00:34:06,440
specifically

310
00:34:06,880 --> 00:34:08,400
waiting for this big fish.

311
00:34:09,550 --> 00:34:10,360
Diana...

312
00:34:11,670 --> 00:34:14,070
That's a major thorn
in Director Li's side.

313
00:34:27,800 --> 00:34:28,730
What do you want?

314
00:34:29,800 --> 00:34:31,650
The Plum Blossom Agency called me,

315
00:34:31,650 --> 00:34:34,440
demanding
that you be dismissed and investigated!

316
00:34:34,440 --> 00:34:35,840
You saved my life.

317
00:34:38,280 --> 00:34:39,610
Whatever you decide...

318
00:34:41,550 --> 00:34:42,710
I'm fine with it.

319
00:34:46,230 --> 00:34:48,139
I want you to live like
a decent human being,

320
00:34:48,139 --> 00:34:50,340
not in the wretched state you're in now!

321
00:34:58,440 --> 00:35:01,550
There used to be a mutt
at the door of Fairy Bath

322
00:35:03,480 --> 00:35:04,480
named Yeller.

323
00:35:07,550 --> 00:35:09,400
I fed it a lot of bones.

324
00:35:11,710 --> 00:35:12,580
That day,

325
00:35:14,360 --> 00:35:16,590
someone shot it dead.

326
00:35:19,710 --> 00:35:20,920
Maybe it was karma.

327
00:35:22,740 --> 00:35:23,940
Because now,

328
00:35:26,190 --> 00:35:27,840
I'm worse off than it was.

329
00:35:29,360 --> 00:35:30,320
It's dead.

330
00:35:30,710 --> 00:35:31,840
You're still alive!

331
00:35:35,440 --> 00:35:37,640
I went to such great lengths to save you,

332
00:35:38,070 --> 00:35:39,600
and this is how you repay me?

333
00:35:48,320 --> 00:35:50,000
You thought you could
hide your woman away and live

334
00:35:50,000 --> 00:35:51,510
your cozy little life
without anyone knowing?

335
00:35:51,510 --> 00:35:53,040
If I hadn't covered for you—

336
00:35:53,920 --> 00:35:55,320
harboring an NBIS agent,

337
00:35:55,400 --> 00:35:56,800
releasing prisoners without authorization,

338
00:35:56,800 --> 00:35:57,670
and colluding with the NBIS—

339
00:35:57,670 --> 00:35:59,000
any one of those offenses

340
00:35:59,000 --> 00:36:01,530
coming to light
would have gotten you killed!

341
00:36:03,440 --> 00:36:04,960
I know every little trick

342
00:36:06,280 --> 00:36:07,590
you've all pulled.

343
00:36:09,230 --> 00:36:12,030
If I hadn't sent Cang Guanglian
to rescue you,

344
00:36:12,150 --> 00:36:15,880
you'd have been killed in a hail of gunfire
from the Hurricane Team!

345
00:36:19,920 --> 00:36:21,710
I promoted you to this position

346
00:36:22,150 --> 00:36:24,950
because I admire
your ability and determination!

347
00:36:27,800 --> 00:36:29,440
Not to take in a mad dog.

348
00:36:36,230 --> 00:36:37,890
How did I get to this position?

349
00:36:39,880 --> 00:36:40,710
It's fate.

350
00:36:44,010 --> 00:36:45,870
You think promotions and success

351
00:36:46,000 --> 00:36:47,600
come purely through effort?

352
00:36:48,550 --> 00:36:51,080
If so, you'll
spend your whole life suffering.

353
00:36:51,080 --> 00:36:52,280
There are many things

354
00:36:52,590 --> 00:36:54,650
that no amount of effort will get you!

355
00:36:56,510 --> 00:36:58,770
Just like you and that female NBIS agent.

356
00:37:00,320 --> 00:37:01,980
You two didn't have that fate.

357
00:37:06,910 --> 00:37:08,240
I don't believe in fate.

358
00:37:09,960 --> 00:37:11,320
I don't believe in fate!

359
00:37:11,760 --> 00:37:12,730
You don't believe in fate,

360
00:37:12,730 --> 00:37:14,530
but you still have to stay alive!

361
00:37:27,110 --> 00:37:27,840
Tomorrow.

362
00:37:29,130 --> 00:37:31,770
A Communist suspect
is coming from Jiaxing to Shanghai

363
00:37:31,770 --> 00:37:32,970
to meet a key figure.

364
00:37:34,590 --> 00:37:36,250
Handle this matter properly,

365
00:37:37,110 --> 00:37:39,670
and maybe I can still plead
with the Plum Blossom Agency

366
00:37:39,670 --> 00:37:40,670
to save your life.

367
00:37:42,920 --> 00:37:44,380
If you lost your position,

368
00:37:45,320 --> 00:37:47,190
you'd really be that dog, Yeller.

369
00:37:49,150 --> 00:37:51,150
How would you get your revenge then?

370
00:38:03,130 --> 00:38:03,560
Hello.

371
00:38:03,580 --> 00:38:04,250
It's me.

372
00:38:06,000 --> 00:38:06,710
Director.

373
00:38:08,360 --> 00:38:09,110
Send 2 men

374
00:38:10,000 --> 00:38:12,460
to the train station
to pick up a guest for me.

375
00:38:13,210 --> 00:38:14,670
He'll be coming from Hangzhou,

376
00:38:14,670 --> 00:38:15,760
arriving at 1 PM,

377
00:38:16,000 --> 00:38:17,260
wearing a gray fedora.

378
00:38:18,310 --> 00:38:19,710
Where should we take him?

379
00:38:20,360 --> 00:38:21,820
Wherever the guest wants.

380
00:38:22,360 --> 00:38:23,090
Understood.

381
00:38:29,620 --> 00:38:31,680
Everyone's glad you're back on duty.

382
00:38:32,230 --> 00:38:33,760
Especially Captain Cang.

383
00:38:34,670 --> 00:38:37,200
He's beaming,
as bright as flowers in spring.

384
00:38:37,950 --> 00:38:39,830
He's gloating.

385
00:38:42,440 --> 00:38:43,840
Really? I couldn't tell.

386
00:38:44,920 --> 00:38:47,650
I'm practically
at the mercy of the Japanese now.

387
00:38:47,880 --> 00:38:50,680
They're all waiting to
see me make a fool of myself.

388
00:38:51,550 --> 00:38:54,480
I absolutely refuse to
give them that satisfaction.

389
00:38:57,400 --> 00:38:58,150
Come with me.

390
00:38:59,590 --> 00:39:00,190
What for?

391
00:39:00,730 --> 00:39:01,590
To catch someone.

392
00:39:01,590 --> 00:39:02,240
Now?

393
00:39:04,510 --> 00:39:05,570
It's getting late.

394
00:39:07,550 --> 00:39:08,640
I'll go get my camera.

395
00:39:08,640 --> 00:39:09,290
Wait.

396
00:39:09,820 --> 00:39:10,900
Bring your gun too.

397
00:39:11,670 --> 00:39:12,840
Didn't you say

398
00:39:13,190 --> 00:39:15,280
I just need to be a photographer?

399
00:39:15,480 --> 00:39:17,210
I don't think that way anymore.

400
00:39:17,950 --> 00:39:19,020
We have to

401
00:39:19,400 --> 00:39:21,330
fight our way to a future of our own.

402
00:39:31,360 --> 00:39:32,750
Captain Du, Mr. Chen,

403
00:39:33,070 --> 00:39:34,000
off on a mission?

404
00:39:34,670 --> 00:39:35,800
Just a small errand.

405
00:39:36,190 --> 00:39:38,190
Then I wish you both the best of luck.

406
00:40:28,920 --> 00:40:32,050
Section Chief Zhao,
we've arrived at the train station.

407
00:40:35,510 --> 00:40:44,220
[Station Exit]

408
00:41:02,000 --> 00:41:04,130
Zhao Qian, General Affairs Division.

409
00:41:11,510 --> 00:41:13,360
Lu Xiaoguang, Hangzhou

410
00:41:13,900 --> 00:41:15,500
No. 76 Operations Division.

411
00:41:16,030 --> 00:41:17,030
Section Chief Lu,

412
00:41:17,630 --> 00:41:19,090
I've heard a lot about you.

413
00:41:19,510 --> 00:41:20,320
Director Li has instructed us

414
00:41:20,320 --> 00:41:21,370
to take you wherever you want.

415
00:41:21,370 --> 00:41:22,430
Where should we go?

416
00:41:26,890 --> 00:41:29,150
To Feiyang Teahouse in Changding Alley.

417
00:42:17,550 --> 00:42:18,670
It's freezing.

418
00:42:19,150 --> 00:42:20,680
Should we close the window?

419
00:42:21,550 --> 00:42:22,240
Don't.

420
00:42:23,150 --> 00:42:24,550
The view outside is nice.

421
00:42:38,110 --> 00:42:39,880
Do you think
this Communist code-named Diana

422
00:42:39,880 --> 00:42:41,280
is a man or a woman?

423
00:42:43,550 --> 00:42:44,550
Who is Diana?

424
00:42:46,230 --> 00:42:50,290
The person in charge of the Communist Party's
Shanghai Liaison Station.

425
00:42:50,670 --> 00:42:52,440
Today's mission is to catch her?

426
00:42:52,440 --> 00:42:54,440
Yes, a big fish.
